<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III, Prince of Salm-Kyrburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III, Prince of Salm-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyrburg">Kyrburg</a>, was a German prince who lived mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, where he built the Hôtel de Salm, now the Palace of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> of Honour. He sympathised with the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a> but was arrested during the Terror and guillotined in July 1794. His son Frederick IV later ruled the Principality of Salm.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-prince-of-salm-kyrburg.jpg" alt="Frederick III, Prince of Salm-Kyrburg" width="139" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_III_of_Salm-Kyrburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
